WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.050
Crackle.

2
00:00:01.100 --> 00:00:06.020
An invented flight, Skylark forty-two,
asks the control tower for permission to

3
00:00:06.070 --> 00:00:07.010
climb.

4
00:00:07.060 --> 00:00:09.230
The tower answers: yes.

5
00:00:09.280 --> 00:00:13.010
But the word dissolves into
static, and never arrives.

6
00:00:13.060 --> 00:00:15.150
A longer reply crackles too.

7
00:00:15.200 --> 00:00:17.890
The pilot waits, and asks again.

8
00:00:17.940 --> 00:00:23.240
So why are pilots trained to say
affirm, and not yes, or affirmative?

9
00:00:23.290 --> 00:00:27.030
In this mission, you'll meet
the radio words pilots must use,

10
00:00:27.080 --> 00:00:29.510
and ask why the rules are so strict.

11
00:00:29.560 --> 00:00:33.530
You'll compare other jobs too, from
the cockpit to the doctor's surgery,

12
00:00:33.580 --> 00:00:36.070
and ask what drives the way they talk.

13
00:00:36.120 --> 00:00:39.710
Your mission: work out
why pilots say affirm.
